{
    "id": 54,
    "title": "Data cleanup, the rest: drop-offs as their own kind, the crawler's gate on cleanup's checks, drop-off pins",
    "why": "Jason, 2026-11-15 (in chat): \"for the rest of the build make one release so i can check it all at once\", choosing all three follow-ups of release #52. (1) Drop-offs as their own kind: places that aren't businesses (PlaceScope::NOT_A_BUSINESS: the Mail & package drop-off category) stay out of business browse lists (the directory's browsing when no words are typed, a town's sections and essentials) while typed searches, the map and choosing the kind still find them; they can't be claimed (Claims::start refuses with the reason; the listing page shows 'nothing to claim' with Suggest an edit; claim.php opens Suggest an edit instead, never a dead end). (2) The crawler's gate (AutoImport::evaluate) uses Data cleanup's junkName(), so page text is held for a person, with its reason, instead of going live; nothing runs while automation is paused. (3) Pins: a drop-off's pin is its own point, from its street address by the U.S. Census geocoder (free, as every listing's point; Data cleanup's 'Place 25 on the map', a person's press); OpenStreetMap's post boxes and package lockers are a new kind of its layer ('dropoff', named from their operator when unnamed), shown in search as its own credited layer and never copied onto our listings (decisions/0065, so not 'from OSM' as first offered). FAQ: the drop-off entry and the staff entry updated. Built on Sync 2026-11-15 01:39 UTC.",
